Most of my promising Valks end up dying from choking (though my latest
YASDed by stepping onto a polyorph trap outside Medusa's place (turned
into a kobold) and getting drowned by an eel). After a while of killing
everything in sight, you start to feel invincible, not thinking about
how much you've eaten. There comes a point in the night that the "y"
button starts looking a lot like the "n" button...

Troll corpses are especial offenders in the choking dept--I start
getting low on HP, it almost seems like death either way.

Though I wouldn't recommend saccing troll corpses you need to get rid
of--another of my recent YASDs was an Olog-Hai resurrecting out of my
inventory on the way to the altar.

On the other hand, if you have a good AC and plenty of HP, the whole
resurrecting thing might be a good way to keep a heavy corpse fresh, if
you killed it a ways from the altar...



